Doesn't it?

00:00:45.061 --> 00:00:46.546
- Ew, it's slimy.

00:00:46.546 --> 00:00:47.627
- I don't like that it's wet.

00:00:47.627 --> 00:00:50.181
- Mmm,mm,mm,mm,mm,mm.

00:00:50.181 --> 00:00:51.666
- It feels like a bean.

00:00:51.666 --> 00:00:52.966
- It's salty,

00:00:52.966 --> 00:00:54.243
and it's (bleep) (mumbles).

00:00:54.243 --> 00:00:55.428
- I like it a lot.

00:00:55.428 --> 00:00:56.485
- I am pleasantly surprised.

00:00:56.485 --> 00:00:57.750
I am not gonna lie.

00:00:57.750 --> 00:00:59.270
- [Voiceover] Liver mush.

00:00:59.270 --> 00:01:01.070
It looks like burnt toast.

00:01:01.070 --> 00:01:03.937
- A weird brownie, that's
what it feels like.

00:01:03.937 --> 00:01:05.098
- It smells pretty good.

00:01:05.098 --> 00:01:06.398
- I'm not mad at it.

00:01:06.398 --> 00:01:07.896
Maybe it would be would be
with ketchup or like a sauce.

00:01:07.896 --> 00:01:08.697
- You're not mad at it?

00:01:08.697 --> 00:01:09.417
- Uh-uh.

00:01:09.417 --> 00:01:12.831
- Yeah, it's like a sandier
cousin of the hamburger.

00:01:12.831 --> 00:01:15.291
- I could see myself cuttin'
open one of these biscuits,

00:01:15.291 --> 00:01:16.301
putting it in there.

00:01:16.301 --> 00:01:17.578
- Can you give us like five minutes?

00:01:17.578 --> 00:01:18.659
I just wanna finish eating.

00:01:18.659 --> 00:01:20.178
- [Voiceover] Country ham

00:01:20.178 --> 00:01:20.899
- [Voiceover] Country ham.

00:01:20.899 --> 00:01:22.002
- [Voiceover] Country ham.

00:01:22.002 --> 00:01:25.218
- It's not your typical deli
ham you see in the supermarket.

00:01:25.218 --> 00:01:26.627
- This is like

00:01:27.165 --> 00:01:28.143
ham.

00:01:28.143 --> 00:01:29.862
- You guys are on some
next level (bleep) here.

00:01:29.862 --> 00:01:31.440
- It's like a hug from the Lord.

00:01:31.440 --> 00:01:32.194
It's delicious.

00:01:32.194 --> 00:01:33.041
- Mm.

00:01:33.041 --> 00:01:34.458
- [both] Mm, mm, mm.

00:01:34.458 --> 00:01:36.316
Mm, mm, mm.

00:01:36.316 --> 00:01:38.033
- What would happen if I
replaced my morning coffee

00:01:38.033 --> 00:01:39.276
with this gravy?

00:01:39.276 --> 00:01:40.796
- Oh here's something that tastes good.

00:01:40.796 --> 00:01:41.620
I know what we'll do.

00:01:41.620 --> 00:01:43.340
We'll soak it in butter and gravy.

00:01:43.340 --> 00:01:44.894
Oh, you're a genius.

00:01:44.894 --> 00:01:47.379
- [woman with long brown
hair] Oh it's a moon pie.

00:01:47.379 --> 00:01:48.239
- (bleep) yes.

00:01:48.239 --> 00:01:49.133
- Oh my (bleep).

00:01:49.133 --> 00:01:49.957
- (bleep) yes.

00:01:49.957 --> 00:01:51.639
- Who needs something this big?

00:01:51.639 --> 00:01:53.057
There's like three cookies in one.

00:01:53.057 --> 00:01:55.111
- Looks like a s'mores on steroids.

00:01:55.111 --> 00:01:57.039
- Oh, try and take this away from me.

00:01:57.039 --> 00:01:59.221
- That's probably the
thickest cookie I've ever had.

00:01:59.221 --> 00:02:00.115
- It's a lot to bite into.

00:02:00.115 --> 00:02:03.412
- I could see like every
third grader in the south

00:02:03.412 --> 00:02:06.360
